 "policy_profile": "t24-mysql-resource-group",
 "description": "T24 MySQL CPU resource-group lifecycle (issue #103): CREATE/ALTER/DROP RESOURCE GROUP reach kind=ddl with audited semantics under MySQL — a dedicated MySQLResourceGroupDeclaration (TYPE required on CREATE, VCPU list/range members, THREAD_PRIORITY bounds -20..19 with SYSTEM -20..0 and USER 0..19, ENABLE|DISABLE, FORCE on ALTER/DROP) kept strictly separate from the TiDB RU declaration; the version premise (MySQL 8.0+) is a proven-refusal gate (a proven 5.7 refuses every lifecycle statement, an unproven version owes unknown_resource_group_version); the reserved usr_default/sys_default pair provably exists only under a proven 8.0+ version; duplicate option kinds, >64-char names, and static priority/type violations are static refusals; proven duplicate create / absent alter / absent drop refuse while unproven targets owe unknown_resource_group_state plus bounded unknown_host_vcpu_count (declared VCPU) and unknown_resource_group_privilege premises; proven refusals suppress lifecycle notices; FORCE and VCPU warn only on declared evidence. Bare DROP RESOURCE GROUP <name> — the shared form — binds the MySQL registry under MySQL; DROP ... FORCE claims the MySQL carrier; SET RESOURCE GROUP ... FOR stays a bounded unaudited feature under MySQL and a vendor boundary under TiDB; every MySQL CPU form under TiDB and every TiDB RU form under MySQL stays a vendor boundary. metadata_cases encode native probes — none has run and none may be claimed as native PASS.",
